{
  "company_name": "TransRoute Logistics",
  "industry": "Logistics",
  "use_case": "Route planning, fuel optimization, and delivery efficiency",
  "space_title": "TransRoute Logistics - Route Planning & Delivery Efficiency 🗺️",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Logistics\n\n**Use case:** Route Planning, Fuel Optimization & Delivery Efficiency\n\nTransRoute Logistics — segment-level route analytics across 28 mixed-fleet vehicles (Semi / Truck / Van) and 10 metro depots. VP Logistics and Fleet Managers use the space to spot underperforming lanes and overweight-empty miles; the S&OP Lead and CFO use it to manage fuel spend, OTIF performance, and CO2 disclosure for scope-1 reporting.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Fuel cost per km (USD) — primary driver of variable cost; benchmark $0.18–$0.30/km for diesel semis\n- Load utilization % — capacity fill rate; <70% signals deadhead / under-loading exposure\n- On-time delivery % — customer SLA metric; 95%+ is industry target\n- Fuel efficiency (km / liter) — operating ratio and ESG metric\n- Cost per delivery (USD) — unit economics for pricing and margin analysis\n- Traffic delay minutes — congestion / route-quality indicator\n- CO2 emissions (kg) — scope-1 reporting and customer ESG asks\n- Total distance km — exposure base for all per-km ratios\n\n**Data sources**\n- `vehicles` — fleet master (type, capacity, fuel, home depot, status) for 28 assets\n- `route_segments` — daily segment-level records with distance, fuel, load, traffic, weather\n- `route_efficiency_metrics` — weekly rollups per vehicle: distance, fuel, OTD, cost per delivery, CO2",
  "schema_basename": "route_planning",
